\paragraph{Neural end-to-end baselines.}
DeBERTa-v3-base (LoRA, 53--61\%) and RoBERTa-DCOL (ordinal contrastive, 64.5\%) lag RF by 14--25\,pp; implications are discussed in \S\ref{sec:discussion}.

\paragraph{Binary detectors and membership inference.}
Perturbation-based (DetectGPT, 28.8\%) and membership-inference (Min-K\% Prob, 33.2\%) methods produce scores with no ordinal resolution (Table~\ref{tab:baselines}); Binoculars d1v2 AUC\,=\,0.50--0.53 vs.\ RF 0.93 (Appendix~\ref{app:detector_baselines}).
Binoculars \cite{binoculars2024}, calibrated with 11-feature RF, independently converges to 78.1\% ($p{>}0.05$ vs.\ 78.4\%; merged 30-feature: 82.6\%; Appendix~\ref{app:feature_ablation_bino}).
